#: ../../../genex/JOIN.rst:2
msgid "JOIN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../manual/include/GENEX_FAMILY.rst:3
msgid ""
"This generator expression belongs to the |genex-family| family. See that "
"section for related generator expressions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/JOIN.rst:8
msgid "$<JOIN:list,glue>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../genex/JOIN.rst:12
msgid ""
"Joins the ``list`` with the content of the ``glue`` string inserted between "
"each item.  This is conceptually the same operation "
"as :genex:`$<LIST:JOIN,list,glue> <LIST:JOIN>`, but the two have different "
"behavior with regard to empty items. :genex:`$<LIST:JOIN,list,glue> "
"<LIST:JOIN>` preserves all empty items, whereas ``$<JOIN:list,glue>`` drops "
"all empty items from the list."
msgstr ""
